#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid "double-barrel derringer"
msgid_plural "double-barrel derringers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "double-barrel derringer" of gun "Bond Arms
#. Derringer"
#. ~ Description of variant "Bond Arms Derringer" of item "double-barrel
#. derringer"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid ""
"Derringers are old-fashioned conceal carry weapons, usually sporting one or "
"two barrels.  The Bond Arms Derringer is a modern series of multi-barrel "
"compact pistols.  Most commonly chambered for .45 Colt, with chambers long "
"enough to accept .410 shotgun shells.  Though, with modern handguns, "
"derringers have become less and less practical as a conceal carry option."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid "cowboy six-shooter"
msgid_plural "cowboy six-shooters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "cowboy six-shooter"
#. ~ Description of "cowboy six-shooter"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid ""
"A reproduction of an antique firearm, chambered in .45 Colt.  Due to the lack"
" of a swing-out cylinder, each cartridge must be reloaded and ejected "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "cowboy six-shooter"
#. ~ Variant name of item "cowboy six-shooter"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid "Colt Single Action Army"
msgid_plural "Colt Single Action Armies"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "cowboy six-shooter" of gun "Colt Single Action
#. Army"
#. ~ Description of variant "Colt Single Action Army" of item "cowboy six-
#. shooter"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid ""
"A famous revolver for many westerns, the Colt Single Action Army has seen "
"plenty of military service, production ends, and production restarts.  While "
"originally in a large amount of chamberings, it is mostly found in .45 Colt "
"chamberings today.  While reloading is slow due to the lack of a swing-out "
"cylinder, it was still much faster than earlier revolvers of the time thanks "
"to using metallic cartridges.  It's also sometimes referred to as the "
"Peacemaker, Model P, M1873 or shortened to SAA."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "cowboy six-shooter"
#. ~ Variant name of item "cowboy six-shooter"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid "Uberti 1873 Cattleman"
msgid_plural "Uberti 1873 Cattlemans"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "cowboy six-shooter" of gun "Uberti 1873 Cattleman"
#. ~ Description of variant "Uberti 1873 Cattleman" of item "cowboy six-
#. shooter"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid ""
"This 7.5\" barreled Uberti Cattleman is a modern reproduction of the "
"legendary Colt Single Action Army, or Colt Peacemaker, one of the first "
"revolvers to use a modern self-contained cartridge.  Made famous by Westerns,"
" it is still in demand for Cowboy Action Shooting, reenactors, and "
"collectors.  Unlike modern revolvers, the cylinder cannot swing out for "
"loading, and spent brass must be ejected one at a time."
msgstr ""

